  871 f52e:             ;
  872 f52e:             ; ---- Video card driver: the video card V3 (YACC1-D 2026-11-11, branch video-v3) ------------------------------------
  873 f52e:             ; The picture is 640 x 480 dots in the HD63484's frame buffer, drawn by the chip from commands: 16-bit words through
  874 f52e:             ; its write FIFO (OUT PB with the address register 0), the high byte first. The chip is busy for milliseconds on a
  875 f52e:             ; clear or a scroll and the FIFO holds 16 bytes, a byte more is lost: every command goes after the status shows the
  876 f52e:             ; FIFO empty (vwfe), 16 bytes at most at a time. V I copies the font from the card's EPROM into frame buffer RAM under
  877 f52e:             ; the screen, as a picture of the 96 glyphs of $20-$7F in three rows of 32 (tools/v3font.py); a character is then one
  878 f52e:             ; graphic copy (AGCPY) of its 8 x 16 dots from x = (code and $1F) x 8, y = -1 - 16 x its row, to the chip's current
  879 f52e:             ; pointer, which the copy leaves at the next cell. Cursor: VROW/VCOL, and VYTOP = the Y of the row's top line (the
  880 f52e:             ; chip's Y runs up: 479 for row 0, 16 less a row). vputc handles CR (column 0), LF (column 0 of the next row: Y1/OS
  881 f52e:             ; ends lines with LF alone), BS (one left, no erase), TAB (spaces to the next multiple of 8), FF (clear + home);
  882 f52e:             ; other control bytes and DEL are ignored; a character in the last column wraps; LF on the last row scrolls (the chip
  883 f52e:             ; copies the screen up a row and clears the last). Only instructions of the 2021 set: no LDZ/STZ/ADDIW/SHL16/BRUR,
  884 f52e:             ; no R2.
  885 f52e:             ;
  886 f52e:             ; vidreset: at reset. Mirroring off, the cursor variables home, probe; with VIDAUTO also V I + mirroring on.
  887 f52e:             vidreset:
  888 f52e: 0e 00               LDAI 0
  889 f530: e5 0f f1            STA VIDMIR
  890 f533: e5 0f f2            STA VIDCUR
  891 f536: e5 0f f3            STA VROW
  892 f539: e5 0f f4            STA VCOL
  893 f53c: 0e 50               LDAI VCOLS
  894 f53e: e5 0f f8            STA VCOLSV
  895 f541: 1f 01 df            MVIW R7,VYHOME
  896 f544: ef 0f f6            STR R7,VYTOP
  897 f547: 04 f5 5e            JSR vprobe
  898 f54a: 0e 00               LDAI VIDAUTO
  899 f54c: a1 f5 5d            BRZ vidrx
  900 f54f: e4 0f f0            LDA VIDPRES
  901 f552: a1 f5 5d            BRZ vidrx
  902 f555: 04 f5 91            JSR vinit
  903 f558: 0e 01               LDAI 1
