 1132 f6f0:             ; ---- V: the video unit (monitor command) ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 1133 f6f0:             ; V then a letter (blanks skipped); numbers are hex, blanks between them optional. V? (or any other letter) lists:
 1134 f6f0:             ;   VS  status          VP  probe again      VI  start the chip, the font, clear, home     VC  clear, home
 1135 f6f0:             ;   VM1 / VM0  mirror on / off               VW rr cc text  the cursor to row rr, column cc and the text there
 1136 f6f0:             ;   VR rr [vv]  write the chip's register byte rr, or read it     VX hh hh ..  bytes to the chip's write FIFO
